IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc8-part8-murder.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART VIII: sections 229 to 240 (murder, manslaughter and infanticide; punishment).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc8-part7-houses.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING). "when" / "where" conditions that fail answer JUST FALSE (marginal reading M2).
-- The answer other parts ask of this one is `s 231 the kind of homicide offence` (a MAYBE of the core `Kind of homicide offence`; PLAN.md section 6, seam of ccc27 for ss 745 to 746.1).
-- Section 2 answers a rule turns on enter as inputs named `by s 2 <term>`; offences named by section number are tested against the core `Provision of the Code` (seam rule R1).

§ `Section 229 -- Murder`

-- src:4511 | 229 Culpable homicide is murder
-- src:4512 | (a) where the person who causes the death of a human being
-- src:4513 | (i) means to cause his death, or
-- src:4514 | (ii) means to cause him bodily harm that he knows is likely to cause his death, and is reckless whether death ensues or not;
-- src:4515 | (b) where a person, meaning to cause death to a human being or meaning to cause him bodily harm that he knows is likely to cause his death, and being reckless whether death ensues or not, by accident or mistake causes death to another human being, notwithstanding that he does not mean to cause death or bodily harm to that human being; or
-- src:4516 | (c) if a person, for an unlawful object, does anything that they know is likely to cause death, and by doing so causes the death of a human being, even if they desire to effect their object without causing death or bodily harm to any human being.
@ref s 229 (src:4511-4516)
GIVEN `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person who causes the death of a human being means to cause his death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person means to cause him bodily harm that he knows is likely to cause his death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reckless whether death ensues or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person, meaning to cause death to a human being or meaning to cause him bodily harm that he knows is likely to cause his death, and being reckless whether death ensues or not, by accident or mistake causes death to another human being` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person, for an unlawful object, does anything that they know is likely to cause death, and by doing so causes the death of a human being` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229 culpable homicide is murder` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND (   `the person who causes the death of a human being means to cause his death`
                OR (`the person means to cause him bodily harm that he knows is likely to cause his death` AND `the person is reckless whether death ensues or not`)
                OR `a person, meaning to cause death to a human being or meaning to cause him bodily harm that he knows is likely to cause his death, and being reckless whether death ensues or not, by accident or mistake causes death to another human being`
                OR `a person, for an unlawful object, does anything that they know is likely to cause death, and by doing so causes the death of a human being`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Culpable homicide is murder (a) where ... (b) where ... or (c) if ..." (a "where" / "if" condition: marginal reading M2)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Culpable homicide is murder" (the section speaks only of culpable homicide)

§ `Section 231 -- Classification of murder`

-- src:4521 | (2) Murder is first degree murder when it is planned and deliberate.
@ref s 231(2) (src:4521-4521)
GIVEN `it is planned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is deliberate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(2) the murder is first degree murder` MEANS
    IF `it is planned` AND `it is deliberate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Murder is first degree murder when it is planned and deliberate" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4523 | (3) Without limiting the generality of subsection (2), murder is planned and deliberate when it is committed pursuant to an arrangement under which money or anything of value passes or is intended to pass from one person to another, or is promised by one person to another, as consideration for that other’s causing or assisting in causing the death of anyone or counselling another person to do any act causing or assisting in causing that death.
@ref s 231(3) (src:4523-4523)
GIVEN `it is committed pursuant to an arrangement under which money or anything of value passes or is intended to pass from one person to another, or is promised by one person to another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is as consideration for that other's causing or assisting in causing the death of anyone or counselling another person to do any act causing or assisting in causing that death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(3) the murder is planned and deliberate` MEANS
    IF `it is committed pursuant to an arrangement under which money or anything of value passes or is intended to pass from one person to another, or is promised by one person to another` AND `that is as consideration for that other's causing or assisting in causing the death of anyone or counselling another person to do any act causing or assisting in causing that death`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without limiting the generality of subsection (2), murder is planned and deliberate when it is committed pursuant to an arrangement" (subsection (2) still speaks of any planned and deliberate murder)

-- src:4526 | (4) Irrespective of whether a murder is planned and deliberate on the part of any person, murder is first degree murder when the victim is
-- src:4527 | (a) a police officer, police constable, constable, sheriff, deputy sheriff, sheriff’s officer or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace, acting in the course of his duties;
-- src:4528 | (b) a warden, deputy warden, instructor, keeper, jailer, guard or other officer or a permanent employee of a prison, acting in the course of his duties; or
-- src:4529 | (c) a person working in a prison with the permission of the prison authorities and acting in the course of his work therein.
@ref s 231(4) (src:4526-4529)
GIVEN `the victim is a police officer, police constable, constable, sheriff, deputy sheriff, sheriff's officer or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim is a warden, deputy warden, instructor, keeper, jailer, guard or other officer or a permanent employee of a prison` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim is a person working in a prison with the permission of the prison authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim was acting in the course of his duties or, for a person working in a prison with permission, in the course of his work therein` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(4) the murder is first degree murder because of the victim` MEANS
    IF (`the victim is a police officer, police constable, constable, sheriff, deputy sheriff, sheriff's officer or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace` OR `the victim is a warden, deputy warden, instructor, keeper, jailer, guard or other officer or a permanent employee of a prison` OR `the victim is a person working in a prison with the permission of the prison authorities`) AND `the victim was acting in the course of his duties or, for a person working in a prison with permission, in the course of his work therein`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "murder is first degree murder when the victim is (a) a police officer ... acting in the course of his duties; (b) a warden ... acting in the course of his duties; or (c) a person working in a prison ... acting in the course of his work therein" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4531 | (5) Irrespective of whether a murder is planned and deliberate on the part of any person, murder is first degree murder in respect of a person when the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an offence under one of the following sections:
-- src:4532 | (a) section 76 (hijacking an aircraft);
-- src:4533 | (b) section 271 (sexual assault);
-- src:4534 | (c) section 272 (sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm);
-- src:4535 | (d) section 273 (aggravated sexual assault);
-- src:4536 | (e) section 279 (kidnapping and forcible confinement); or
-- src:4537 | (f) section 279.1 (hostage taking).
@ref s 231(5) (src:4531-4537)
GIVEN `the offence the person was committing or attempting to commit` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(5) the murder is first degree murder because of the offence being committed` MEANS
    IF `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit that offence` AND elem (`the offence the person was committing or attempting to commit`'s `section`) (LIST 76, 271, 272, 273, 279, 279.1)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "murder is first degree murder in respect of a person when the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an offence under one of the following sections: (a) section 76 ... (f) section 279.1" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4539 | (5.1) Irrespective of whether a murder is planned and deliberate on the part of any person, murder is first degree murder when the death is caused by that person
-- src:4540 | (a) while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim’s physical or psychological safety is threatened, in the case where the victim is that person’s intimate partner;
-- src:4541 | (b) while exercising control, direction or influence over the movements of the victim with intent to exploit the victim, within the meaning of section 279.04;
-- src:4542 | (c) while committing or attempting to commit an offence of a sexual nature or an offence for a sexual purpose; or
-- src:4543 | (d) while motivated by hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or mental or physical disability.
@ref s 231(5.1) (src:4539-4543)
GIVEN `the death is caused while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim's physical or psychological safety is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim is that person's intimate partner, by s 2 intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the death is caused while exercising control, direction or influence over the movements of the victim with intent to exploit the victim, within the meaning of section 279.04` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the death is caused while committing or attempting to commit an offence of a sexual nature or an offence for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the death is caused while motivated by hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(5.1) the murder is first degree murder because of the circumstances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the death is caused while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim's physical or psychological safety is threatened` AND `the victim is that person's intimate partner, by s 2 intimate partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           OR `the death is caused while exercising control, direction or influence over the movements of the victim with intent to exploit the victim, within the meaning of section 279.04`
           OR `the death is caused while committing or attempting to commit an offence of a sexual nature or an offence for a sexual purpose`
           OR `the death is caused while motivated by hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or mental or physical disability`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the death is caused while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim's physical or psychological safety is threatened` AND `the victim is that person's intimate partner, by s 2 intimate partner` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of section 2 "intimate partner" is itself not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "murder is first degree murder when the death is caused by that person (a) while engaging in ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ..." (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4545 | (6) Irrespective of whether a murder is planned and deliberate on the part of any person, murder is first degree murder when the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment) with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim’s physical or psychological safety, or the physical or psychological safety of anyone known to the victim, is threatened.
@ref s 231(6) (src:4545-4545)
GIVEN `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an offence under section 264` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim's physical or psychological safety, or the physical or psychological safety of anyone known to the victim, is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(6) the murder is first degree murder because of criminal harassment` MEANS
    IF `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an offence under section 264` AND `it is with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim's physical or psychological safety, or the physical or psychological safety of anyone known to the victim, is threatened`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "murder is first degree murder when the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment) with intent to cause the victim to believe" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4547 | (6.01) Irrespective of whether a murder is planned and deliberate on the part of a person, murder is first degree murder when the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament if the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity.
@ref s 231(6.01) (src:4547-4547)
GIVEN `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, by s 2 terrorist activity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(6.01) the murder is first degree murder because of terrorist activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament` AND `the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, by s 2 terrorist activity` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament` AND `the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, by s 2 terrorist activity` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of section 2 "terrorist activity" is itself not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "murder is first degree murder when the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence ... if the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4549 | (6.1) Irrespective of whether a murder is planned and deliberate on the part of a person, murder is first degree murder when
-- src:4550 | (a) the death is caused by that person for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization; or
-- src:4551 | (b) the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization.
@ref s 231(6.1) (src:4549-4551)
GIVEN `the death is caused by that person for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(6.1) the murder is first degree murder because of a criminal organization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the death is caused by that person for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the death is caused by that person for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "murder is first degree murder when (a) the death is caused by that person for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization; or (b) ..." (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an answer of section 2 "criminal organization" is itself not covered

-- src:4553 | (6.2) Irrespective of whether a murder is planned and deliberate on the part of a person, murder is first degree murder when the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an offence under section 423.1.
@ref s 231(6.2) (src:4553-4553)
GIVEN `the offence the person was committing or attempting to commit` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(6.2) the murder is first degree murder because of intimidation` MEANS
    IF `the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit that offence` AND (`the offence the person was committing or attempting to commit`'s `section`) EQUALS 423.1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "murder is first degree murder when the death is caused by that person while committing or attempting to commit an offence under section 423.1" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4555 | (7) All murder that is not first degree murder is second degree murder.
@ref s 231(7) (src:4555-4555)
GIVEN `it is murder, by s 229` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is first degree murder, by any of s 231(2) to (6.2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(7) the murder is second degree murder` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is murder, by s 229` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it is first degree murder, by any of s 231(2) to (6.2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is murder, by s 229` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it is first degree murder, by any of s 231(2) to (6.2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "All murder that is not first degree murder is second degree murder" (first degree murder is not second degree murder)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All murder that is not first degree murder" (the section speaks only of murder, and an answer taken from section 229 or from the first degree provisions is itself not covered)

-- src:4519 | 231 (1) Murder is first degree murder or second degree murder.
@ref s 231(1) (src:4519-4519)
GIVEN `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is murder, by s 229, after any reduction under s 232(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is infanticide, by s 233` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answers of the routes to first degree murder, by s 231(2), (4), (5), (5.1), (6), (6.01), (6.1) and (6.2)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of homicide offence`
`s 231 the kind of homicide offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): sections 229 to 234 classify culpable homicide only
        IF `it is infanticide, by s 233` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST infanticide
        IF `it is murder, by s 229, after any reduction under s 232(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND any (GIVEN route YIELD route EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers of the routes to first degree murder, by s 231(2), (4), (5), (5.1), (6), (6.01), (6.1) and (6.2)`
        THEN JUST `first degree murder`
        IF `it is murder, by s 229, after any reduction under s 232(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND all (GIVEN route YIELD route EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the answers of the routes to first degree murder, by s 231(2), (4), (5), (5.1), (6), (6.01), (6.1) and (6.2)`
        THEN JUST `second degree murder`
        IF `it is murder, by s 229, after any reduction under s 232(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `it is infanticide, by s 233` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST manslaughter
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an answer taken from another provision is itself not covered, so the kind is not decided

§ `Section 232 -- Murder reduced to manslaughter`

-- src:4559 | (2) Conduct of the victim that would constitute an indictable offence under this Act that is punishable by five or more years of imprisonment and that is of such a nature as to be sufficient to deprive an ordinary person of the power of self-control is provocation for the purposes of this section, if the accused acted on it on the sudden and before there was time for their passion to cool.
@ref s 232(2) (src:4559-4559)
GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment of the indictable offence that the conduct of the victim would constitute` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(2) the offence is punishable by five or more years of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment of the indictable offence that the conduct of the victim would constitute`
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN
        JUST (IF term's `less a day` THEN (term's years TIMES 12 PLUS term's months) GREATER THAN 60 ELSE (term's years TIMES 12 PLUS term's months) AT LEAST 60)
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): no maximum imprisonment is stated for the offence

-- src:4561 | (3) For the purposes of this section, the questions
-- src:4562 | (a) whether the conduct of the victim amounted to provocation under subsection (2), and
-- src:4563 | (b) whether the accused was deprived of the power of self-control by the provocation that he alleges he received,
-- src:4564 | are questions of fact, but no one shall be deemed to have given provocation to another by doing anything that he had a legal right to do, or by doing anything that the accused incited him to do in order to provide the accused with an excuse for causing death or bodily harm to any human being.
@ref s 232(3) (src:4561-4564)
GIVEN `the victim did something that he had a legal right to do` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim did something that the accused incited him to do in order to provide the accused with an excuse for causing death or bodily harm to any human being` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(3) the victim is deemed to have given provocation` MEANS
    IF `the victim did something that he had a legal right to do` OR `the victim did something that the accused incited him to do in order to provide the accused with an excuse for causing death or bodily harm to any human being`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no one shall be deemed to have given provocation to another by doing anything that he had a legal right to do, or by doing anything that the accused incited him to do in order to provide the accused with an excuse for causing death or bodily harm to any human being"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no one shall be deemed to have given provocation to another by doing anything that"

@ref s 232(3) (src:4561-4564)
GIVEN `the question is whether the conduct of the victim amounted to provocation under subsection (2), or whether the accused was deprived of the power of self-control by the provocation that he alleges he received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(3) the question is a question of fact` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether the conduct of the victim amounted to provocation under subsection (2), or whether the accused was deprived of the power of self-control by the provocation that he alleges he received`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the questions (a) whether the conduct of the victim amounted to provocation ... and (b) whether the accused was deprived of the power of self-control ... are questions of fact"

-- src:4559 | (2) Conduct of the victim that would constitute an indictable offence under this Act that is punishable by five or more years of imprisonment and that is of such a nature as to be sufficient to deprive an ordinary person of the power of self-control is provocation for the purposes of this section, if the accused acted on it on the sudden and before there was time for their passion to cool.
@ref s 232(2) (the provocation) (src:4559-4559)
GIVEN `the conduct of the victim would constitute an indictable offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that offence is punishable by five or more years of imprisonment, by s 232(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is of such a nature as to be sufficient to deprive an ordinary person of the power of self-control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused acted on it on the sudden` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused acted before there was time for their passion to cool` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim is deemed to have given provocation, by s 232(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(2) the conduct of the victim is provocation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the victim is deemed to have given provocation, by s 232(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no one shall be deemed to have given provocation to another by doing anything that he had a legal right to do" (subsection (3))
        IF `the conduct of the victim would constitute an indictable offence under this Act` AND `that offence is punishable by five or more years of imprisonment, by s 232(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the conduct is of such a nature as to be sufficient to deprive an ordinary person of the power of self-control` AND `the accused acted on it on the sudden` AND `the accused acted before there was time for their passion to cool`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `that offence is punishable by five or more years of imprisonment, by s 232(2)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): no maximum imprisonment is stated for the offence
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is provocation for the purposes of this section, if the accused acted on it on the sudden and before there was time for their passion to cool" (an "if" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4557 | 232 (1) Culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder may be reduced to manslaughter if the person who committed it did so in the heat of passion caused by sudden provocation.
@ref s 232(1) (src:4557-4557)
GIVEN `it is culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder, by s 229` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person did so in the heat of passion caused by sudden provocation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was provocation, by s 232(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(1) the culpable homicide is reduced to manslaughter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder, by s 229` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person did so in the heat of passion caused by sudden provocation` AND `there was provocation, by s 232(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder, by s 229` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (NOT `the person did so in the heat of passion caused by sudden provocation`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be reduced to manslaughter if the person who committed it did so in the heat of passion caused by sudden provocation" (an "if" condition: marginal reading M2)
        IF `it is culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder, by s 229` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `there was provocation, by s 232(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person who committed it did so in the heat of passion caused by sudden provocation" (provocation as subsection (2) defines it)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder may be reduced to manslaughter"

-- src:4566 | (4) Culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder is not necessarily manslaughter by reason only that it was committed by a person who was being arrested illegally, but the fact that the illegality of the arrest was known to the accused may be evidence of provocation for the purpose of this section.
@ref s 232(4) (src:4566-4566)
GIVEN `it is culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was committed by a person who was being arrested illegally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(4) the homicide is manslaughter by reason only that the person was being arrested illegally` MEANS
    IF `it is culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder` AND `it was committed by a person who was being arrested illegally`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Culpable homicide that otherwise would be murder is not necessarily manslaughter by reason only that it was committed by a person who was being arrested illegally"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not necessarily manslaughter by reason only that"

@ref s 232(4) (the knowledge) (src:4566-4566)
GIVEN `it was committed by a person who was being arrested illegally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the illegality of the arrest was known to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(4) the knowledge of the illegality of the arrest may be evidence of provocation` MEANS
    IF `it was committed by a person who was being arrested illegally` AND `the illegality of the arrest was known to the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the fact that the illegality of the arrest was known to the accused may be evidence of provocation"

§ `Sections 233 and 234 -- Infanticide and manslaughter`

-- src:4568 | 233 A female person commits infanticide when by a wilful act or omission she causes the death of her newly-born child, if at the time of the act or omission she is not fully recovered from the effects of giving birth to the child and by reason thereof or of the effect of lactation consequent on the birth of the child her mind is then disturbed.
@ref s 233 (src:4568-4568)
GIVEN `the person is a female person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by a wilful act or omission she causes the death of her newly-born child, by s 2 newly-born child` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the act or omission she is not fully recovered from the effects of giving birth to the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason thereof or of the effect of lactation consequent on the birth of the child her mind is then disturbed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233 the female person commits infanticide` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a female person` AND `by a wilful act or omission she causes the death of her newly-born child, by s 2 newly-born child` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `at the time of the act or omission she is not fully recovered from the effects of giving birth to the child` AND `by reason thereof or of the effect of lactation consequent on the birth of the child her mind is then disturbed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is a female person` AND `by a wilful act or omission she causes the death of her newly-born child, by s 2 newly-born child` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of section 2 "newly-born child" is itself not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A female person commits infanticide when by a wilful act or omission she causes the death of her newly-born child, if at the time of the act or omission she is not fully recovered" (a "when" and "if" condition: marginal reading M2; a person who is not a female person also answers JUST FALSE here, not NOTHING, because this function defines the category that s 231 and s 234 consume: marginal reading M8, fork F15)

-- src:4570 | 234 Culpable homicide that is not murder or infanticide is manslaughter.
@ref s 234 (src:4570-4570)
GIVEN `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is murder, by s 229, after any reduction under s 232(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is infanticide, by s 233` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234 the culpable homicide is manslaughter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it is murder, by s 229, after any reduction under s 232(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `it is infanticide, by s 233` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`it is murder, by s 229, after any reduction under s 232(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `it is infanticide, by s 233` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Culpable homicide that is not murder or infanticide is manslaughter" (murder and infanticide are not manslaughter)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Culpable homicide that is not murder or infanticide" (the section speaks only of culpable homicide, and an answer taken from sections 229 or 233 may itself be not covered)

§ `Sections 235 to 240 -- Punishment`

