-- src:4580 | (2) The court that imposes a sentence for manslaughter shall consider imposing a sentence of imprisonment for life if the person committed the manslaughter
-- src:4581 | (a) while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim’s physical or psychological safety is threatened, in the case where the victim is that person’s intimate partner;
-- src:4582 | (b) while exercising control, direction or influence over the movements of the victim with intent to exploit the victim, within the meaning of section 279.04;
-- src:4583 | (c) while committing or attempting to commit an offence of a sexual nature or an offence for a sexual purpose; or
-- src:4584 | (d) while motivated by hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or mental or physical disability.
@ref s 236(2) (src:4580-4584)
GIVEN `the person committed the manslaughter while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim's physical or psychological safety is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim is that person's intimate partner, by s 2 intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person committed the manslaughter while exercising control, direction or influence over the movements of the victim with intent to exploit the victim, within the meaning of section 279.04` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person committed the manslaughter while committing or attempting to commit an offence of a sexual nature or an offence for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person committed the manslaughter while motivated by hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(2) the court shall consider imposing a sentence of imprisonment for life` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person committed the manslaughter while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim's physical or psychological safety is threatened` AND `the victim is that person's intimate partner, by s 2 intimate partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           OR `the person committed the manslaughter while exercising control, direction or influence over the movements of the victim with intent to exploit the victim, within the meaning of section 279.04`
           OR `the person committed the manslaughter while committing or attempting to commit an offence of a sexual nature or an offence for a sexual purpose`
           OR `the person committed the manslaughter while motivated by hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or mental or physical disability`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person committed the manslaughter while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct with intent to cause the victim to believe that the victim's physical or psychological safety is threatened` AND `the victim is that person's intimate partner, by s 2 intimate partner` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of section 2 "intimate partner" is itself not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall consider imposing a sentence of imprisonment for life if the person committed the manslaughter (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ..." (an "if" condition: marginal reading M2)

@ref s 236(2) (src:4580-4584)
DECLARE `s 236(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 236(2) consider imposing a sentence of imprisonment for life`

@ref s 236(2) (src:4580-4584)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 236(2) act`
`s 236(2) the duty of the court to consider imposing a sentence of imprisonment for life` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 236(2) consider imposing a sentence of imprisonment for life`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 236(2): the court did not consider imposing a sentence of imprisonment for life"

