§ `Section 239 -- Attempt to commit murder`

-- src:4601 | (2) In determining, for the purpose of paragraph (1)(a), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:4602 | (a) an offence under this section;
-- src:4603 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244 or 244.2; or
-- src:4604 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:4605 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref s 239(2) (src:4601-4605)
-- Fork F10: "10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody":
-- the ten years are counted from the day of the earlier conviction by `add years`, and every day in custody between the two convictions postpones the end of the period by one day.
GIVEN `the earlier offence of which the person was convicted` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
      `the number of days spent in custody between those two days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(2) the earlier conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the earlier offence is one of those listed` AND `ten years have elapsed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody"
        IF `the earlier offence is one of those listed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence" (the text lists what is considered; it does not say that nothing else is)
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS `the earlier offence of which the person was convicted`'s `section`
        `the subsection` MEANS `the earlier offence of which the person was convicted`'s `subsection`
        `the earlier offence is one of those listed` MEANS
               `the section` EQUALS 239
            OR (`the section` EQUALS 85 AND (`the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR `the section` EQUALS 244
            OR `the section` EQUALS 244.2
            OR (elem `the section` (LIST 220, 236, 272, 273, 279.1, 344, 346) AND `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence`)
            OR (`the section` EQUALS 279 AND `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" AND `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence`)
        `ten years have elapsed` MEANS
            `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` AT LEAST (`add years` `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` 10 PLUS `the number of days spent in custody between those two days`)

-- src:4607 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction.
@ref s 239(3) (src:4607-4607)
GIVEN `the question is whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence for the purposes of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(3) the sequence of commission of offences is to be considered` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence for the purposes of subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (2)"

