@ref s 239(1) (src:4594-4599)
GIVEN `the answers of s 239(2) for each earlier conviction of the person` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1)(a) the offence is a first offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN earlier YIELD earlier EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers of s 239(2) for each earlier conviction of the person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence" (an earlier offence is to be considered)
        IF all (GIVEN earlier YIELD earlier EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the answers of s 239(2) for each earlier conviction of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an answer of subsection (2) is itself not covered

