-- src:4594 | 239 (1) Every person who attempts by any means to commit murder is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:4595 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if any firearm is used in the commission of the offence and the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:4596 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:4597 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years;
-- src:4598 | (a.1) in any other case where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years; and
-- src:4599 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 239(1) (the limbs) (src:4594-4599)
GIVEN `a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a first offence, by s 239(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 239(1) the limb that applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` OR (`any firearm is used in the commission of the offence` AND `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND `it is a first offence, by s 239(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 239(1)(a)(i) five years`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
        IF (`a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` OR (`any firearm is used in the commission of the offence` AND `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND `it is a first offence, by s 239(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 239(1)(a)(ii) seven years`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
        IF (`a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` OR (`any firearm is used in the commission of the offence` AND `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND `it is a first offence, by s 239(1)(a)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether it is a first offence is not covered
        IF `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence`
        THEN JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 239(1)(a.1) four years`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
        OTHERWISE JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

@ref s 239(1) (the limbs) (src:4594-4599)
GIVEN `the limb that applies, by s 239(1)` IS A MAYBE Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 239(1) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limb that applies, by s 239(1)`
    WHEN JUST limb THEN LIST limb
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY   -- the limb is not covered: the empty list is the "not covered" value here (the caller sees `s 239(1) the limb that applies` answer NOTHING)

-- src:4609 | 240 Every one who is an accessory after the fact to murder is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 240 (src:4609-4609)
GIVEN `the person is an accessory after the fact to murder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240 the person commits the offence of being an accessory after the fact to murder` MEANS
    IF `the person is an accessory after the fact to murder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who is an accessory after the fact to murder is guilty of an indictable offence" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 240 (src:4609-4609)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 240 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 240 (src:4609-4609)
`s 240 the limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 240 (src:4609-4609)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 240 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 240 the limb`
